# Impeccable Overdrive Rules

Overdrive is for rare, high-impact UI moments that should feel extraordinary.

It is not for normal UI polish.

## Core Principle

Pick one important moment and make it exceptional.

Do not spread spectacle across the whole interface.

## When To Use

Use Overdrive for:

- Landing hero sections
- Premium first impressions
- High-value CTA transitions
- Special showcase interactions
- Important storytelling moments

For this travel website, Overdrive may be used for:

- Home hero section
- Featured destination reveal
- Destination detail hero image
- AI recommendation entry point in future versions

## When NOT To Use

Do not use Overdrive for:

- Dashboards
- Admin pages
- Forms that need reliability
- Search/filter controls
- Basic destination cards
- Every page or every section

Reliability beats spectacle in functional UI.

## Techniques

Use advanced techniques only when justified:

- cinematic transitions
- scroll-based reveals
- mouse-position responsive effects
- GPU-friendly transforms
- canvas/WebGL effects
- spring-like motion
- view transitions

Prefer simple CSS/Tailwind first.

Only add libraries if the effect truly needs them.

## Performance Rules

Overdrive must feel smooth.

- Target 60fps
- Use transform and opacity when possible
- Avoid layout thrashing
- Avoid heavy animation on many elements
- Profile performance if effects feel slow
- Cut the effect if it hurts usability

Slow spectacle is worse than simple design.

## Reduced Motion

Reduced-motion fallback is mandatory.

Always respect users who prefer reduced motion.

If complex animation is used, provide a clean static fallback.

## Restraint

- Overdrive should be rare
- One cinematic moment is enough
- Do not animate everything
- Do not make UI feel like a demo reel

## Travel Website Application

Good Overdrive ideas:

- Hero image with subtle cinematic parallax
- Destination hero reveal with soft mask animation
- Featured destination cards entering with stagger
- CTA transition from home to destinations
- Ambient gradient background behind hero only

Bad Overdrive ideas:

- Every card animates aggressively
- Filters use complex animation
- Page becomes slower
- Motion distracts from travel content

## Constraints

- Do not change business logic
- Do not break search/filter/sort
- Do not add heavy dependencies unless necessary
- Keep fallback UI simple
- Keep code understandable for a beginner when possible

## Goal

The UI should feel:

- memorable
- cinematic
- smooth
- premium
- intentional
